    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T00:27:09Z",
    "body": "Already done - no code needed. The per-brick update cost law exists and is asserted in the debug lane: `crates/sim/tests/stock_field_cost.rs` (commit 8b5fb82e, \"a cut costs only its own bricks (M7.3 A)\"). Its four tests are:\n- `a_far_move_touches_its_own_footprint_not_the_grid`: the work doesn't grow with the grid, and the bricks visited stay inside the tool's own box.\n- `a_batch_visits_each_brick_once_and_answers_the_same`\n- `an_emptied_brick_is_skipped_whole`\n- `a_long_move_pays_only_inside_the_stock`\n\nThe app heavy lane (`crates/app/tests/stock_field_cost.rs`) reports the per-program numbers and points to this law. My #26 research missed it; correcting that here. Unclaiming. This can close as already done (8b5fb82e). I can't close issues from this account, so it's left for the maintainer.",
